# Recursive Flint — findings by Nemotron 3.5 Super VL 120B A12B

> Source: Recursive Superintelligence (flint)
> Date: 2026-10-25 (UTC)
> Overview and scoring methodology: ../../model-comparison.md
> Cross-model signed log: ../../model-findings.md

## Model card

- **Name:** Recursive Flint
- **Short description:** Open-weight mixture-of-experts model built for fast agentic coding on local hardware; 40B total / ~2.5B active parameters per token.
- **Provider / access:** Hugging Face (`RecursiveSI/flint`, `RecursiveSI/flint-nvfp4-gguf`), llama.cpp, Ollama, Unsloth, LM Studio, vLLM, SGLang, Recursive's `rec` inference engine. Apache 2.0 license.
- **Release / knowledge:** Released 2026-10-21. Knowledge cutoff not stated.
- **IDs:** `RecursiveSI/flint` (HF).
- **Context window:** Up to 512k tokens (vendor); 262,144 tokens (vLLM/FreshContext); recommends staying within 256k for best results.
- **Modalities:** Text in; text out. Reasoning model (emits GLM-4.7-style tool calls and thinking blocks). Tool calling supported.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-25):** Open weights (Apache 2.0, self-hosted; no per-token API pricing found).
- **Architecture:** 40B total / ~2.5B active MoE; 49-layer pre-norm MoE, hidden size 2048, 256 experts (sigmoid top-6 + shared expert), 35 sliding-window layers (window 513) + 14 full-attention layers, 4 KV heads, GQA with 32 query heads. NVFP4 quantized checkpoint (GGUF) alongside BF16. Built with Recursive's Eureka Machine automated research system.

### Raw benchmarks found

- SWE-bench Verified: **74.2%** measured (recursive.com release evals, benchgap measured, MindStudio, FreshContext)
- SWE-bench Pro v2: **89.7%** measured (recursive.com, MindStudio, FreshContext) vs **51.9%** estimated ±4.6 pp (benchgap) — major conflict between vendor-measured and model-estimated scores
- Terminal-Bench 2.1: **54.9%** measured (recursive.com, benchgap measured, MindStudio, FreshContext)
- LiveCodeBench v6: **80.3%** measured (benchgap); vendor mentions it in average but no specific number
- IFBench: **89.2%** measured (benchgap); vendor mentions in average
- IFEval: **95.1%** measured (benchgap); vendor mentions in average
- SciCode: **45.4%** estimated ±3.4 pp (benchgap); AA-SciCode **45.7%** estimated ±3.9 pp
- AA Coding Index: **48.3%** estimated ±5.3 pp (benchgap)
- FreshContext own tests: screening 98.3%, grounding 77.6%, nullschema 70.8%, toolcall 55.0%, toolscale 95.0%, contract 60.4%, needle 60.0%
- Speed: 125+ tok/s on M4 Pro MacBook Pro, 150+ tok/s on RTX Spark (vendor); ~500 tok/s on GB200, 485 tok/s batch-1 at 100K context (vLLM); 74.2 t/s single-stream decode (FreshContext)

### Normalized scores (1–100)

- Tool use: **78/100.** Strong tool-calling suite (toolscale 95%, toolcall 55% in FreshContext); emits GLM-4.7-style tool calls; capped by low unprompted tool invocation (2/12 when tool holds answer).
- Reasoning: **82/100.** Strong coding reasoning (SWE-bench Verified 74.2%, SWE-bench Pro v2 89.7%, Terminal-Bench 2.1 54.9%); SWE-bench Pro v2 conflict (89.7% vendor vs 51.9% benchgap estimate) tempers confidence.
- Context window: **75/100.** 262K–512K tokens; FreshContext measured 26.4GB peak RSS at 64K context, fits on single consumer/prosumer GPU.
- Multimodal: **15/100.** Text-only input/output (template minimum for text-only models).
- Coding: **88/100.** Headline coding model; SWE-bench Verified 74.2%, SWE-bench Pro v2 89.7%, LiveCodeBench v6 80.3%; leads sub-50B MoE models on agentic coding benchmarks per vendor.
- Cost efficiency: **85/100.** Apache 2.0 open weights (free to self-host), ~2.5B active params enables fast local inference; BF16 checkpoint ~80GB requires substantial hardware.
- **Overall Score: 81/100.** Half-up mean of the five non-cost dims; best-fit recommendation: local, self-hosted agentic coding agent where open weights and fast inference matter more than multimodal capability.

